<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peribsen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2700 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/28th-century-bce">28th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peribsen was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-dynasty-of-egypt">Second Dynasty of Egypt</a>, around 2700 BCE. Unusually, he placed the animal of the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seth">Seth</a> rather than the falcon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horus">Horus</a> above his royal name, which may reflect religious or political division in the country. He was buried at Abydos, and his reign remains poorly understood.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peribsen.jpg" alt="Peribsen" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iry-Hor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peribsen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
